      "stageRecord": "Comprou raises from the established V position into the transitive light verb, creating a complex head. Its lower occurrence becomes unpronounced. Que then undergoes Internal Merge at the outer edge of the transitive v domain, outside the agent. This intermediate occurrence is required by the phase-based analysis: subsequent relative extraction must proceed from the accessible edge rather than directly from the transferred verbal complement. The lower object copy is unpronounced, while the edge copy temporarily carries que's pronunciation. Finite T subsequently merges above this completed v object. Head movement and operator movement have independent targets; both precede this Merge of T.",
